   Recent talk regarding the potential new Soldier class has reminded me of an 
old idea of mine -- the Minstrel class.
   The Minstrel would begin with low strength and constitution and a high 
dexterity, intelligence, and charisma.  Armor would be a cockscomb (the funny
hat jesters wear).  I can't think of any appropriate weapon, though a 
quarterstaff might do.  The Minstrel would also begin with a magical instrument
such as a magic whistle, magic flute, magic harp, fire horn, frost horn, or
drum of earthquakes.  In addition, the Minstrel would start with a blessed 
spellbook of taming, and maybe a scroll of taming, too.
   The Minstrel should not begin with a mere dog or cat as a pet.  Instead, the
pet should be chosen from a list of unusual creatures such as tigers, bears,
apes, and wolves.  (You could instead just assign a totally random creature, as
is done for polymorph, but this would be overly cruel to the hacker assigned a 
freezing sphere as a pet.)


